  "status_text": "Go around the circle in one direction and you need to keep four readings in play. Work from both ends and one is enough. Put sixteen sensors in a ring, labelled A through H and then H back through A. Matching letters share a report bit. At each step count the letters with one sensor visited and one still waiting. Any one-way walk has at least four open pairs at some point. Start at the two A's and take each matching pair in turn. The count never goes above one. Lean checked the exact savings for every ring of this form (L-lib-1051).",
